  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are orthonormal.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $Q$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it is square.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
